      "writtenOn": "2013-11-26T16:07:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ok, but then you have a race condition between gpio_enable_interrupt and gpio_disable_interrupt on the same block.\n\nTASK1                                                                  TASK2\ngpio_disable_interrupt(\nMEC1322_INT_DISABLE(girq_id) |\u003d (1 \u003c\u003c bit_id);\t\nif (!MEC1322_INT_ENABLE(girq_id))\n\n                                                                           gpio_enable_interrupt(\n                                                                           MEC1322_INT_ENABLE(girq_id) |\u003d (1 \u003c\u003c bit_id);\n                                                                           MEC1322_INT_BLK_EN |\u003d (1 \u003c\u003c girq_id);\n\nMEC1322_INT_BLK_DIS |\u003d (1 \u003c\u003c girq_id);\n\n\u003d\u003d\u003e the block ends up disable while it should be enable.\nIs this optimization useful (for no looping somewhere ? for power ?) else we can just remove it.",
